. Where a Redistribution licence(s) is listed on the Order Form, the Customer is granted a licence to:
2.4.1.1. redistribute the Data to End Customers via Devices in accordance with clause 3 below;
2.4.1.2. use the Trade Marks to support marketing of the service, and to meet attribution requirements as further described below;
and
2.4.1.3. use, store, process and make available the Data as part of the Customer’s services in accordance with the terms of the
Agreement.

. A Private Investor is an End Customer who is not required to be regulated or supervised by a body concerned with the regulation or
supervision of investment or financial services and who meets all the conditions set out below:
3.2.2.1. The End Customer subscribes (i.e., registers and pays) in a personal capacity;
3.2.2.2. The End Customer is not currently registered or qualified as a professional securities trader or investment adviser with any
national or state exchange, regulatory authority, professional association or recognised professional body;
3.2.2.3. The End Customer does not currently act in any capacity as an investment adviser, regardless of if they have previously been
qualified to do so;
3.2.2.4. The End Customer uses the service solely in relation to the management of their personal funds;
3.2.2.5. The End Customer does not redistribute, republish, or otherwise provide any Data from the service to any third party in any
manner or use or process Data for any commercial purpose; and
3.2.2.6. The Data Charge is designed to cover individuals and will be maintained in the End Customer’s name and not in the company
name – the exception to this would be a share club operating on a non-professional basis.

. The Last Trade Price Data consists solely of Real Time Data for:
3.9.3.1. instrument name;
3.9.3.2. instrument identifier(s) – e.g., ISIN and/or SEDOL;
3.9.3.3. last traded price for that instrument;
3.9.3.4. volume of shares traded in that transaction; and
3.9.3.5. time of the trade.

. The Last Trade Price licence:
3.9.4.1. restricts the dissemination of Last Trade Price Data within limited Website data services technically controlled by the
Redistributor;
3.9.4.2. only permits interactive functionality using Last Trade Price Data contained within those Website services;
3.9.4.3. does not permit the redistribution of Last Trade Price Data to Professional Users; and
3.9.4.4. does not permit the onward dissemination or exporting of Data via API or any other redistribution channel.

. Redistributors can appoint Service Facilitators to sell and/or deliver Real Time Data in a closed user group environment
(“Redistribution Service Facilitator”). To be deemed eligible, the following criteria must be met (unless otherwise approved in writing
by the Exchange):
5.1.1.1. The Redistributor must contract directly with the End Customer in respect of the Data delivery, and such contract must be in
place prior to Data enablement;
5.1.1.2. The Redistributor is wholly responsible for compliance with the Reporting Schedule and the Audit Schedule;
5.1.1.3. The Redistributor must allocate Unique User IDs;
5.1.1.4. The Redistribution Service Facilitator is permitted to modify and/or database the Data, solely where such use is always in
support of the Redistributor’s provision of Data to its End Customers;
5.1.1.5. The Redistribution Service Facilitator is forbidden in its contract with the Redistributor from providing Data to any customers
who are not customers of the Redistributor (other than as an approved Redistribution Service Facilitator for other
Redistributors or as a Redistributor in its own right);
5.1.1.6. The Redistribution Service Facilitator, in its contract with the Redistributor, agrees to the same terms as the Redistributor in
respect of market data audits, and is also subject to audit by the Redistributor;
5.1.1.7. Where the Brand on the Data service is exclusively that of the Redistributor, and 5.1.1.1 - 5.1.1.6 are met, no additional
licensing is required. Where the Brand is not exclusively of the Redistributor, and 5.1.1.1- 5.1.1.6 are met, Redistribution
Service Facilitator Licence Charges apply for each Data Product for each Redistribution Service Facilitator, and such
Redistribution Service Facilitator must be listed on the Order Form.

. Members are eligible for discounted Data Charges as outlined in the Price List and Data Product Schedule in respect of the following
Data Products:
7.5.1.1. UK market Data Level 2;
7.5.1.2. UK market Data Level 1;
7.5.1.3. International market Level 2; and
7.5.1.4. International market Level 1.

. A Redistributor may grant a one-off, single free trial of 30 days during which no Data Charges will apply. This will apply:
7.6.1.1. Per Natural User for display Devices;
7.6.1.2. Per End Customer location for Data delivered via datafeed.
